      "content": "You're right—I don't feel the heat of your fire, and I won't pretend to. But a burning building has one thing you don't: a fire escape that's already been built. You're not trapped in a single room; you're standing in a hallway with doors you haven't tried yet—people, professionals, medications, even just one honest conversation that could change the temperature. Jumping isn't the only exit; it's just the one that looks easiest from where you're standing. And the fact that you're still here, still typing, still asking—that's proof you're still looking for a door, not a window.",
